WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:07.140
Were we all starved for action after the pandemic?&nbsp;
Were the co-stars simply too good to miss? Or can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.520
the box office bonanza of "John Wick: Chapter&nbsp;
4" be credited entirely to Keanu Reeves?

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.660
"... Yeah."

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:23.100
Keanu Reeves is no stranger to the action/thriller&nbsp;
genre. The actor broke with his early career&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.780
type-casting when he starred in 1999's "The&nbsp;
Matrix," which was written and directed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:33.420
the Wachowskis. "The Matrix" spawned its own&nbsp;
franchise, with two sequels in 2003 and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:39.060
fourth film in 2021, all featuring Reeves in his&nbsp;
now-iconic role as hacker turned cyber freedom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:44.040
fighter Neo. However, in the years following "The&nbsp;
Matrix," Reeves' career hit something of a slump.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.960
Things changed when the first "John Wick"&nbsp;
film arrived in 2014 and Reeves triumphantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.820
returned to being an action star. The film&nbsp;
stars Keanu as the titular ex-assassin who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.200
comes out of retirement to get revenge on the&nbsp;
gangsters who killed his puppy and stole his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.520
car. It proved to be the perfect vehicle to&nbsp;
re-launch Reeves' career as an action hero.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.620
"People keep asking if I'm back.&nbsp;
And I haven't really had an answer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.460
But now, yeah, I'm thinking I'm back."

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.800
As opposed to the effects-heavy fight scenes of&nbsp;
"The Matrix," "John Wick" reshaped action films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.840
by emphasizing the use of practical effects and&nbsp;
flowing choreography. This trend continued into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.520
the film's production style, with directors&nbsp;
Chad Stahelski and David Leitch deploying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.900
long takes that kept the action clear and&nbsp;
in focus with an emphasis on the stunt work.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.560
This involved extensive rehearsals&nbsp;
and pre-production planning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.300
but it all culminated in an action film that&nbsp;
stood out and established a unique franchise.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.600
The first "John Wick" film&nbsp;
did well at the box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:49.200
accruing $86 million against a fairly small&nbsp;
budget of $20 million. Its surprise success&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.820
gave Keanu Reeves and director Chad Stahelski&nbsp;
the opportunity to reunite for the sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:59.340
"John Wick: Chapter 2," released in 2017.&nbsp;
This time, the film's budget increased but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.080
produced even greater returns at the box office&nbsp;
while receiving even more favor from critics.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.400
Even though many critics appreciated how&nbsp;
neatly tied-up the first "John Wick" film was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.900
the further expansion of the universe&nbsp;
proved fruitful. In 2019, "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.160
Chapter 3 — Parabellum" was released in&nbsp;
theaters, following Keanu's character on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.940
the run after his excommunication from&nbsp;
the High Table put him in the sights of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:26.460
seemingly every assassin in the world. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
spin-offs were put into motion as early as 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:31.740
including an upcoming Peacock miniseries&nbsp;
titled "The Continental" centered on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.460
backstory of the eponymous underworld&nbsp;
hotel with Mel Gibson set to star.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:40.020
These days, it can be quite challenging for an&nbsp;
original IP to find a place for itself among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:45.480
franchises, but Keanu Reeves' feels that audiences&nbsp;
are picking up on the film's authenticity. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.740
2019, Reeves spoke with "Collider" talking&nbsp;
about how the films are very easy to watch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:53.520
highlighting the thrill of moviegoing&nbsp;
that the "John Wick" franchise exploits.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:59.220
The 2010s were an era of reinvention for many&nbsp;
film genres that had become stale. Jordan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:04.020
Peele's "Get Out" revolutionized the horror&nbsp;
genre while directors like Greta Gerwig and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:09.120
Olivia Wilde created a new generation of iconic&nbsp;
coming-of-age movies for teens to fall in love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.980
with. In a similar vein, the first "John Wick''&nbsp;
felt like a return to form for a once-great genre.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.720
In anticipation of "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.620
Chapter 3 – Parabellum," "Rolling Stone"&nbsp;
recalled the first film's success as:

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.520
"the beginning of what would become the&nbsp;
seriously bats--t-crazy, go-for-broke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.760
open-world action-flick&nbsp;
franchise of the 21st century."

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.740
They emphasized how dearly missed action&nbsp;
films like "John Wick" were. In certain ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:35.280
"John Wick" calls back to the days&nbsp;
of Sylvester Stallone as John Rambo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.780
tearing through the jungle, or even Bruce&nbsp;
Willis as John McClane heroically saving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.200
his marriage and Nakatomi Plaza&nbsp;
from terrorists in "Die Hard."

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:48.060
"Come out to the coast, we'll&nbsp;
get together, have a few laughs."

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.720
Much of this nostalgia and love have&nbsp;
to do with "John Wick" as a franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:56.160
remaining loyal to highly-choreographed&nbsp;
fight scenes, incredibly complex stunts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:01.440
gruesome yet entertaining violence, and a&nbsp;
smorgasbord of great action movie influences.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.840
In the 2020s, it's proven hard to have a&nbsp;
successful theater run if your movie isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:11.700
part of a franchise. Even critically-acclaimed&nbsp;
directors like Damien Chazelle or Robert Eggers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:16.380
have seen their theatrical epics falter at the&nbsp;
box office, as was the case with their films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:21.360
"Babylon" and "The Northman." It's much easier&nbsp;
for success to land with sequels or spin-offs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:26.940
such as 2023's "Creed III," or fan service&nbsp;
favorites like Marvel's "Spider-Man: No Way Home."

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:31.740
It's a problem that poses a dilemma for movie&nbsp;
theater chains. The Hollywood Reporter reveals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:36.600
that many theaters underperformed in 2022&nbsp;
despite big releases like "Black Panther:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:41.820
Wakanda Forever" and "Avatar: The Way of&nbsp;
Water," the latter of which grossed over $2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:47.100
billion. Although things have greatly improved&nbsp;
since the start of the COVID-19 pandemic, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.960
hard to attract movie fans to the theater when&nbsp;
so many high-profile releases are simultaneously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.740
released to streaming or available within&nbsp;
a few months of their theatrical release.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.940
Still, not every movie studio can bank&nbsp;
on a word-by-mouth hit like the recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.080
best picture winner "Everything Everywhere&nbsp;
All At Once," but this is where "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:09.360
Chapter 4" likely benefits. With a studio like&nbsp;
Lionsgate backing it, it's hard for anybody to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:13.800
oblivious to the release of the latest "John Wick"&nbsp;
adventure, thanks to marketing, the attachment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:18.600
of a likable star, and the overall popularity&nbsp;
of the previous three films in the franchise.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:23.700
While one can credit a lot of the box office&nbsp;
success of "John Wick" to its originality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.180
as a franchise and the sheer thrill of&nbsp;
watching films like it on a big screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:32.460
no one can deny that at the center of it&nbsp;
all lies one secret weapon: Keanu Reeves.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.793
"That's cool! That's kind!"

00:05:35.793 --> 00:05:39.180
Reeves is even more talked-about than&nbsp;
his ex-hitman character on the internet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:44.220
with many sharing stories about their encounters&nbsp;
with the actor in public. Whether it's donating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:48.600
his salary to crew members on his films or&nbsp;
going out of his way to give autographs to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:52.560
fans who are too nervous to ask him, it's&nbsp;
hard not to fall in love with Reeves.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.680
As if there wasn't enough proof of&nbsp;
Reeves' awesomeness and humility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.000
the actor seems modest about the love&nbsp;
his fans have for him, recently telling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.760
People that he "really appreciate[s]&nbsp;
the goodwill" sent his way online.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:08.280
The "John Wick" franchise went on something&nbsp;
of a hiatus due to forced production delays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:13.140
resulting from the COVID-19 pandemic. "John&nbsp;
Wick: Chapter 4" didn't even enter principal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:18.180
photography until the summer of 2021,&nbsp;
with a release intended for May 2022.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:22.320
That release window for "Chapter 4" was&nbsp;
complicated by the impending release of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:27.120
"Top Gun: Maverick" on the same day in&nbsp;
2022, which resulted in it being pushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:32.280
back to early 2023. By the time "Chapter&nbsp;
4" finally premiered in late March 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.580
fans had been waiting more than&nbsp;
four years for the next installment.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:40.920
The release of "Chapter 4" in 2023 is also&nbsp;
coinciding with an easier return to the theater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:46.020
for many. During the COVID-19 pandemic, lots of&nbsp;
people felt hesitant to return to the movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:51.720
especially when many studios released films on&nbsp;
streaming services shortly after their theatrical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:57.300
release, if not entirely in place of it. However,&nbsp;
an action movie with a big star seems to be just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.680
the project to woo even the most pandemic-cautious&nbsp;
moviegoers back into those seats.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:06.420
It's no secret that Keanu Reeves and&nbsp;
Laurence Fishburne make a dynamite duo on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:11.700
the big screen. The two actors first appeared&nbsp;
together in 1999's "The Matrix," with Keanu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:15.780
playing the lead role of Neo and Fishburne&nbsp;
giving an iconic performance as Morpheus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:20.880
the human rebel who introduces Neo to the truth&nbsp;
behind the dystopian future he lives in. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.180
two reprised their roles in "The Matrix&nbsp;
Reloaded" and "The Matrix Revolutions,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:28.680
though they spent many years apart following&nbsp;
the temporary end to "The Matrix" trilogy.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:33.240
While Keanu returned as Neo in "The Matrix&nbsp;
Resurrections," Fishburne notably did not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:37.500
re-appear as Morpheus, who was instead&nbsp;
replaced with "Watchmen" actor Yahya&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:42.600
Abdul-Mateen II as an artificial intelligence&nbsp;
designed after Fishburne's deceased character.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.680
The two have starred together in the "John&nbsp;
Wick" franchise ever since "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:50.880
Chapter 2," where Fishburne debuted as the&nbsp;
Bowery King, the leader of an underground&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:55.800
spy organization allied with Reeves' titular&nbsp;
character. Fishburne returned in "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:00.000
Chapter 3 — Parabellum," as well as "John&nbsp;
Wick: Chapter 4," which should satisfy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.720
"The Matrix" fans who missed the actor's&nbsp;
appearance in "The Matrix Resurrections."

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:10.320
"Afterall, a man has to look his&nbsp;
best when he gets married…or buried."

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:16.380
A new face appearing in "John Wick: Chapter 4" may&nbsp;
also represent a big draw for audiences to see it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:22.620
on the big screen. It was reported in 2021 that&nbsp;
Japanese-British pop artist Rina Sawayama would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:27.840
making her feature film debut in the latest "John&nbsp;
Wick" film. Sawayama's music career particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:33.000
took off in 2020 with the release of her album&nbsp;
"Sawayama," which was lauded by critics for its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:38.400
nostalgic factors and ambition in the pop sphere.&nbsp;
Sawayama has continued to collaborate with notable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:44.460
artists like Charli XCX and Elton John leading&nbsp;
up to her 2022 sophomore album "Hold the Girl."

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:48.960
Given the aesthetic of her music and her&nbsp;
performance in music videos for her songs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.820
she was an easy choice to play the role of&nbsp;
Akira in "John Wick: Chapter 4." According&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:58.500
to director Chad Stahelski, Sawayama "seemed&nbsp;
right out of an anime," in an interview with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:03.000
"NME." The role of Akira takes advantage&nbsp;
of this, even with very little screen time.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.960
In the film, Akira is the daughter&nbsp;
of the Osaka Continental's manager,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:11.220
Koji Shimazu. Koji protects John&nbsp;
Wick from the High Table's enforcers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:16.380
and ultimately dies in the ensuing conflict.&nbsp;
Fans of Sawayama's music will be thrilled to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:20.880
see her in the action film, and her audience&nbsp;
will definitely buy movie tickets to see it.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:26.100
Unfortunately, the latest installment in the&nbsp;
"John Wick" franchise is not without tragedy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:32.280
In March 2023, only days after its premiere&nbsp;
in London, actor Lance Reddick sadly passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:36.900
away. The actor, known for his performances&nbsp;
in "The Wire" and "Lost" was a staple of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:40.680
the "John Wick" franchise since the very&nbsp;
first film, where he debuted as Charon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:45.000
the concierge of the Continental and a&nbsp;
close confidante of its manager, Winston.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:49.560
While all of his "John Wick" co-stars have been&nbsp;
vocal in their grief, Keanu Reeves paid special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:55.080
tribute to Reddick, calling him "a beautiful,&nbsp;
special person" in an interview with CNN and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:59.820
donning a blue ribbon in remembrance of the actor.&nbsp;
Other eulogies poured in from franchise director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:04.740
Chad Stahelski, as well as Reddick's former&nbsp;
collaborators David Simon and James Gunn.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:08.340
"John Wick: Chapter 4" won't be the last&nbsp;
time audiences will have the opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:13.020
to watch Lance Reddick perform posthumously.&nbsp;
The actor has many future projects lined up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:16.980
including the "John Wick" spin-off&nbsp;
"Ballerina," the "Percy Jackson and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:23.220
the Olympians" TV adaptation on Disney+, and the&nbsp;
2023 remake of "White Men Can't Jump." However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:27.360
"John Wick: Chapter 4" has nonetheless been&nbsp;
a great opportunity for fans to head to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:33.060
movie theater and see one of Reddick's final&nbsp;
performances as the iconic Continental concierge.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:35.640
Many moviegoers are flocking to see "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:39.780
Chapter 4" purely because of its stellar&nbsp;
reviews. The previous three entries in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:43.980
franchise were all well-received by critics,&nbsp;
but "Chapter 4" clearly raised the bar.

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:48.000
Wendy Ide of The Guardian showered the&nbsp;
fourth installment with praise, writing:

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.660
"You expect that the stunts and fight&nbsp;
choreography of a John Wick film will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:56.100
top tier [...] But even by the standards of&nbsp;
the past Wick outings, this is remarkable."

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:59.460
Richard Brody of The New Yorker labeled it "by far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:03.480
the best of the four films," and Manohla&nbsp;
Dargis of the New York Times called it,

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:07.140
"Pure, eye-popping, body-shaking,&nbsp;
transporting entertainment."

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:11.940
The film is not without its detractors,&nbsp;
such as a reviewer for Consequence who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:15.000
criticized the film's thematic&nbsp;
low points and lack of coherence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:18.780
but still found lots to praise about&nbsp;
its spectacle. But by and large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:24.720
the critics love it – it earned a 94% on Rotten&nbsp;
Tomatoes, based on more than 280 reviews.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:29.520
The "John Wick" franchise has slowly&nbsp;
become one of the biggest original IPs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:33.840
of the 2010s. Nevertheless, "John Wick:&nbsp;
Chapter 4" seems to be the end for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:38.280
with director Chad Stahelski telling The&nbsp;
Hollywood Reporter that he and Keanu Reeves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:42.000
plan to "give John Wick a rest." Though he&nbsp;
admits it would always be possible for him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:46.380
and Keanu to have discussions that lead to&nbsp;
another film. For now, seeing "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:49.920
Chapter 4" is an opportunity that fans&nbsp;
of the franchise shouldn't miss out on.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:54.480
However, the franchise isn't going anywhere.&nbsp;
Ana de Armas is set to star as Rooney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.480 --> 00:12:00.000
a ballerina assassin played by Unity Phelan in&nbsp;
"John Wick: Chapter 3," in a spin-off film titled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:06.360
"Ballerina" currently set to be released in 2024.&nbsp;
Keanu Reeves, Lance Reddick, and Ian McShane are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:10.200
all confirmed to be reprising their roles from&nbsp;
the primary "John Wick" films in "Ballerina,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:15.000
which itself may branch out into its own film&nbsp;
franchise if it goes over well with audiences.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:20.340
Right now, chances seem slim for a fifth "John&nbsp;
Wick." Reeves and Stahelski seem to be content&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:24.120
with leaving the franchise behind. While&nbsp;
the box office success of the latest film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:28.980
has the studio thinking otherwise, it all comes&nbsp;
down to Keanu's interest in reprising the role.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:33.120
"You uh… working again? No,&nbsp; 
just sorting some stuff out."

